In .NET 10 (targeting Android 15 / API 35), `adjustResize` is deprecated because edge-to-edge is enforced by default. The fix is to react to **keyboard insets** instead.

## Recommended approach

In your `MainActivity.cs` or a platform-specific handler, opt into IME inset animations so your layout adjusts automatically:

```csharp
// Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView, new InsetsListener());
}

private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var systemBars = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

        // Apply bottom padding = max of IME or nav bar
        v.SetPadding(
            systemBars.Left, systemBars.Top, systemBars.Right,
            Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBars.Bottom));

        return insets;
    }
}
```

## XAML layout tip

Structure your chat page so the input bar is at the bottom of a `Grid`, not inside a `ScrollView`:

```xml
<Grid RowDefinitions="*, Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" Padding="8">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

## Key points

| .NET 9 (old) | .NET 10 (new) |
|---|---|
| `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` | Handle `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` |
| System resizes window | You apply padding/margin from insets |

The insets listener fires when the keyboard appears/disappears, pushing your input bar up automatically with smooth animation support.
